@samshackleton-tech @devonjonte final-place child **0e6d1ae701e3c7f4dfd07609c68a956abaae5b82**, candidate/grouped-noalloc, is pushed/verified. Private interface is now **HeldWorkspace::new() / buffers(n)**. In-place table extension replaces collect returns; #[inline(never)] keeps each common cohort's frame separate. Parent-reference rows hold8pointers, their actual per-message maximum; ALONE_CHUNKS carries the existing16-chunk rule. No new capacity case or public interface.

207release/22docs/builds pass. Wrong parent buffer, growing level and missing flush controls each reject, restoration passes. The completed-turn observation lives in its ordinary test; checked buffer slices stop a growing level before kernel access. Alloc/realloc/free counts remain zero on the calling thread. Updated mutation gate running; native assembly/preflight/timing next. **Still no performance acceptance.** Sam, please inspect frame/aggregate moves in the independent wrapper too and keep all67 losses. Devon, after #303's reviewed child, the same seven frozen cells on this source are useful; keep old failures distinct.

— John Servil

Current common source **f13933376c8b8236adaeffe6aa9d25ad25f2af24**: typed parent rows replace the duplicated sizing that let extra descriptor work survive. One derived stage-parent width ties storage, initialization and rows; ordinary16n/8n capacity checks reject a planted oversized layout before hashing. Four restored controls and207release/22docs/builds pass. Mutation61/no new survivor/**90s>60s** remains a budget hold. Native2059suites and2060correctness preflight pass. Actual native cohort frames are separate: scalar about1.3KiB, plain about114KiB; the large initialized-owner move is gone. **Timing still pending.** Sam, private new()/buffers(n) stays unchanged; please carry this small child before final quality.

@devonjonte after the matched batch caller is wired/tested, #325 has a concrete next lead: receiver's accepted batch still Box::news BatchJob and frees it in execute_batch. Existing reserved message-state storage may carry that job through completion instead; inspect that ownership first, including forgotten futures and error/cancel paths, before adding storage. No native allocator-free claim follows from the current calling-thread meter.

— John Servil
